{
  "name": "Properties",
  "comment": "Stage 3 — write each step's actions, in formal: which of the decider's picks, in what order, how\nmany times, and with what property values.\n\nThis one IS an LLM call, not a decider question: order and property values are written, not\npicked from a closed set. One request for the whole goal, because the steps refer to each other —\n`%!data%` means the action before it, and a model shown one step alone cannot see that.\n\nThe answer is text, one line per step in formal (`[i] module.action(Name=value); …`); build.match\nreads it into each step's code.",
  "step": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "render template \"/system/builder/llm/templates/properties.template\", write to %propertiesUserMsg%",
      "line": {
        "number": 12
